Classification prompt: Task:


Classify each of the participants listed under "Participants to classify", according to how it is used in the input.

Classes:
In the examples below the entity is marked with #...#.
Per - entities that are human individuals or fictitious human characters and divine entities. Ex. #O rapaz# leu o livro.
Org - entities with an organizational structure (e.g. companies, governments, teams, institutions). Ex. #A EDP# subiu os precos.
Obj - entities that represent any kind of tangible, manmade objects. Ex. O Joao partiu #a cadeira#.
Nat - entities that are not manmade and occur naturally (e.g. animals, plants). Ex. #O cao# mordeu o dono.
Fac - facilities.
Veh - vehicles.
Path - a location that consists of a series of locations; it has the potential for traversal; it can function as a boundary; it has no inherent directionality. Ex. autoestrada A1, nacional 222, rua, rio.
Pl_water - Ex. rio, ribeira, mar, oceano, lago, canal.
Pl_celestial - Ex. sol, lua, Marte, Andromeda.
Pl_mountain - a mountain.
Pl_civil - a political region or administrative area, usually sub-national. Ex. Regiao Autonoma dos Acores, Uniao Europeia, Lisboa, area metropolitana do Porto, Minho.
Pl_country - a country.
Pl_mount_range - a mountain range.
Pl_capital - the capital of a country.
Pl_region - a non-political or non-administrative region. Ex. deserto, ilha.
Pl_state - a first-order administrative division within a country (with ISO 3166-2 codes).
Loc - places that do not fit any of the other Pl_ values (e.g. web pages).
Other - entities that do not fit into the other categories. Ex. O Joao sentiu #um cheiro a queimado#.

